# LF everywhere by default.
#
# Everything this repo produces runs on Linux: the Raspberry Pi, the Docker
# containers, and the OpenWrt puck. Windows is only ever the authoring machine,
# and both editors and PowerShell handle LF fine — so LF is the sensible default
# and CRLF the exception, rather than the other way round.
#
# Without this, `core.autocrlf=true` hands out CRLF working copies on checkout.
# A CRLF shell script fails on OpenWrt's /bin/sh and inside containers with
# errors as unhelpful as "no such file or directory" on a line that plainly
# exists — the trailing \r is swallowed into the interpreter path or argument.
# That is the breakage the `sed -i 's/\r$//'` calls in deploy/ work around.
#
# The index is already LF throughout, so this changes checkout behaviour only.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets — never convert. `text=auto` detects these anyway; listing them
# is belt-and-braces against a misdetection corrupting an image or font.
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.png   binary
*.gif   binary
*.ico   binary
*.svg   text eol=lf
*.ttf   binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.mp3   binary
*.wav   binary
*.ogg   binary

# If a Windows batch file is ever added it must keep CRLF — cmd.exe mis-parses
# labels and goto in LF-terminated scripts. (None exist today.)
*.bat   text eol=crlf
*.cmd   text eol=crlf
